  ### 3. Additional context (if relevant):                                                                              
  - The screening yielded **22 included studies out of 50 (44%)**, which is a reasonable yield for this review and      
  avoids the red flag of zero inclusions.                                                                               
  - Three included studies (6, 9, 31, 40, 50) are flagged with **medium or low confidence**, primarily because the      
  abstract was minimal or randomization was not explicitly described. These should be priority candidates for           
  full-text retrieval to confirm design and eligibility.                                                                
  - Study 47 ("Joint mobilization versus self-exercises for limited glenohumeral joint mobility") was excluded despite  
  its title suggesting an RCT because the abstract describes an observational analysis of treatment factors (frequency  
  of sessions and self-exercise compliance) rather than a randomised comparison of mobilization versus self-exercises.  
  - Study 4 was excluded because both arms received physical therapy (exercise), so the comparison does not isolate     
  manual therapy or exercise effects; it tests an invasive adjunct.                                                     
  - Several methodological chapters and systematic reviews (3, 5, 17, 19, 24, 25, 32, 35, 45, 46) were correctly        
  excluded as non-primary studies.                                                                                      
